course: dictionary
lesson: 12813
title: Emancipated: set free
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Emancipated means set free. Its context gives clues: people who were owned or held down are no longer controlled. «Many enslaved people were emancipated after the Emancipation Proclamation of 1863.» The sentence tells you people were freed from slavery, so emancipated means freed.
explain: Emancipated can also mean freed from rules or limits that kept someone down. «After the new law, women could vote and felt emancipated from old rules that had kept them down.» Swap in the word free: "felt free from old rules that had kept them down." It still makes sense, so you have found the right meaning.
explain: In everyday speech, emancipated can describe someone who is independent and thinks for themselves. «Zara made up her own mind and did not follow the crowd, so she felt emancipated.» The context tells you the meaning, but a dictionary can confirm it when you are not sure.
fact: Emancipated means set free from slavery, or from rules and limits that kept someone down.
fact: In the British Empire, enslaved people were emancipated in 1833.
fact: In the USA, the Emancipation Proclamation of 1863 and the 13th Amendment of 1865 helped to free enslaved people.
fact: Emancipate is the verb: they emancipate, they emancipated, they are emancipating.
fact: Emancipated can also mean independent and free-thinking in everyday speech.
exercise: «Many enslaved people were emancipated after the Emancipation Proclamation of 1863.» What does emancipated mean here? | Given a new car | Sent away to school | *Freed from slavery | Locked in a room
exercise: «After the new law, women could vote and felt emancipated from old rules that had kept them down.» What does emancipated mean in this sentence? | Lost in a crowd | Given a lot of money | Very tired after a long day | *Freed from old rules that kept them down
exercise: «Ellie felt emancipated when she was finally free to make her own choices.» Which word is closest in meaning to emancipated? | Hungry | *Free | Tired | Lost
test: «The enslaved people were emancipated, so they were no longer owned.» What does emancipated mean? | *Freed from slavery | Moved to a new town | Painted a bright colour | Bought for a high price
test: Zara makes up her own mind and does not follow the crowd. Which word fits best? | Annoyed | Exhausted | Hungry | *Emancipated
exam: In which country was the Emancipation Proclamation of 1863 issued? | Brazil | *The USA | Australia | France
